  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered comparisons have valid cell counts and are interpreted using the signed hypothesis direction. The key new candidate is feature_003. H62 asks whether feature_003=1 versus 0 is associated with stronger dependency within feature_010=0; the signed estimate is +0.125, interval [0.051, 0.199]. H63 asks the same question within feature_010=1; the signed estimate is +0.188, interval [0.045, 0.332]. H64 tests whether feature_003 modifies the feature_010 association with a negative-direction interaction; the signed estimate is only +0.063, interval [-0.098, 0.224]. Together, these results are not decisive: H62 is below the threshold, H63 is above the threshold at the point estimate but not at the lower confidence bound, and H64 is compatible with meaningful negative modification but points near zero. Because feature_003 is the only new candidate near the threshold and the formal interaction is not strong, I leave H62 unresolved and active, H63 unresolved and active, and H64 unresolved and deferred. I request independent validation for H63 because it is the only claim in this batch whose point estimate exceeds the 0.15 threshold and the only remaining near-threshold alternative to the already dominant feature_010 association. Validation may either strengthen this conditional feature_003 claim or close it as near-null if the independent estimate is not clearly above threshold.\n\nThe feature_010 effect-modification results continue to argue against many context-dependent extensions of the accepted feature_010 association. H18 tests positive modification by feature_009 median and gives a small positive signed estimate, +0.054, interval [-0.070, 0.179]; I do not accept it because the point estimate is near zero, but its upper bound still exceeds the threshold, so I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than close it definitively. H72 tests positive modification by feature_044 median and gives a negative signed estimate with upper bound