  "narrative": "Response-deadline assessment for H13: H13 claims that feature_010=1 is associated with higher, less negative outcome_001, i.e. weaker composite dependency, than feature_010=0. Discovery R11 is +0.829 composite dependency-score units, 95% Welch interval [0.767, 0.891]. Independent validation R25 is +0.821 with conservative validation interval [0.739, 0.903]. The estimates are already signed to the positive hypothesis direction, so both show a large positive association. The validation lower bound remains far above the 0.15 absolute threshold. I therefore keep H13 accepted and closed. This is the dominant dataset-specific finding: feature_010=1 is associated with substantially weaker composite dependency than feature_010=0. It should not be interpreted as causal, mechanistic, or externally generalizable, and the accepted feature_010 stratified claims are overlapping expressions of this same broad association rather than separate independent effects.\n\nNew validation assessment for H63: H63 asked whether feature_003=1 versus 0 is associated with stronger dependency, i.e. lower outcome_001, within the feature_010=1 subgroup. Discovery R40 was a signed +0.188 with 95% Welch interval [0.045, 0.332], suggestive but not conclusive because the lower bound is below the threshold. Independent validation R51 is only +0.068 with interval [-0.147, 0.283]. The validation point estimate is far below the 0.15 threshold and the interval includes zero, so the independent evidence does not corroborate a scientifically meaningful stronger-dependency effect. I reject H63 and close it. This is scientifically informative because it downgrades the main remaining alternative to feature_010. In the same program, H61 global feature_003 negative-direction estimate is +0.139 [0.065, 0.213], below the absolute threshold; H62 conditional within feature_010=0 is +0.125 [0.051, 0.199], also below the threshold; and the negative-direction interaction H64 is +0.063 [-0.098, 0.224], near zero. I close H61 and H62 as boundary near-null candidates and reject H64 as unsupported. The feature_003 signal does not currently justify further validation.\n\nSupported findings remain centered on feature_010. The global positive association is both discovered and independently validated. Accepted stratified feature_010 contrasts indicate that large positive feature_010 effects are present across several pre-specified strata, including research-signature quartiles, assigned-marker positive strata, and log-persistence quartiles. These stratified claims are useful for showing breadth but should not be repeatedly validated because they overlap substantially with the accepted global association.\n\nNegative or unsupported findings include the opposite feature_010 direction H11; global main effects of the assigned binary markers H4-H6; earlier marker-signature interactions H7-H9; feature_041 global and feature_010=0-stratum claims H19 and H57; several rejected broad binary claims, including feature_031 H42 and feature_001 H44; high-prevalence binary claims H65-H69; feature_046 contrasts H70 and H71; several feature_010 positive interaction claims H14, H15, H17, H25, H27, and H72; and now the feature_003 conditional and interaction claims H63 and H64. The earlier invalid exact continuous comparisons are estimability failures, not null findings.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty is concentrated in many still-untested broad claims and a few near-null deferred interactions. Some feature_010 interaction intervals have upper bounds that touch or barely exceed the threshold, such as H16, H18, and H26, but their point estimates are close to zero and they are multiplicity-sensitive; I do not treat them as supported modifications. The untested active claims include broad binary predictors H20-H23 and H45-H56, categorical contrast H24, feature_010 interactions H28, H29, H58-H60, and H73-H76, and remaining unexplored nominal categories. These comparisons are still useful for discovery but are not close to acceptance unless a large, consistent new candidate emerges.\n\nMost informative next analysis: allocate remaining effort away from feature_003 and overlapping feature_010 strata, and toward broad screening of untested active claims, especially untested binary predictors, untested feature_010 interactions, and estimable high-frequency categorical contrasts such as feature_054, feature_034, feature_059, feature_061, and feature_062 if they meet minimum cell counts. Request validation only for a new non-overlapping candidate whose point estimate exceeds the threshold with credible uncertainty. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset, with residual confounding because the analyses are unadjusted Welch comparisons and with multiplicity risk from the large number of comparisons.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence map after validation of H63. H13/H11: feature_010=1 vs 0 global positive weak-dependency association is accepted and independently validated (+0.829 discovery; +0.821 validation). H30-H40 accepted strata are overlapping expressions of this association; do not repeatedly validate overlapping feature_010 strata. Feature_003 program is downgraded/closed: H61 global +0.139 below threshold; H62 within feature_010=0 +0.125 below threshold; H63 within feature_010=1 discovery +0.188 but validation +0.068 [-0.147, 0.283], rejected; H64 interaction small +0.063, rejected. Avoid further feature_003 validation unless a new independent non-overlapping signal appears. Feature_021/feature_047 appear nonindependent and should not be treated as separate findings. Many feature_010 interactions are null or unresolved near-null (H14, H15, H17, H25, H27, H72; deferred H16, H18, H26). Broad binary and feature_046 contrasts mostly rejected. Next priorities: analyze untested active broad claims H20-H23, H45-H56, categorical H24, feature_010 interactions H28, H29, H58-H60, H73-H76, and possible safe categorical contrasts for feature_054, feature_034, feature_059, feature_061, feature_062 if minimum cells pass. Treat all findings as dataset-specific associations, not causal, mechanistic, or externally generalizable. Keep validating only clearly near-threshold or threshold-exceeding candidates with low multiplicity dependence."
