 "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. Therefore, positive signed estimates support the claimed direction: feature_037=1 corresponds to lower outcome_001 (stronger composite dependency) for its negative-direction claims, whereas feature_010=1 or feature_002=1 corresponds to higher outcome_001 (weaker composite dependency) for its positive-direction claims. H144 gives a signed short-log-PFS feature_037 association of +0.799 with 95% lower bound +0.669. H145 and H146 give long- and short-log-PFS feature_002 associations of +0.875 and +0.673, with lower bounds +0.748 and +0.530. H147 and H148 give older- and younger-age feature_037 associations of +0.717 and +0.854, with lower bounds +0.556 and +0.722. H149 and H150 give older- and younger-age feature_002 associations of +0.790 and +0.797, with lower bounds +0.626 and +0.643. H151 and H152 give older- and younger-age feature_010 associations of +0.867 and +0.801, with lower bounds +0.743 and +0.657. Every signed lower bound exceeds the 0.15-unit practical threshold by a wide margin, and the estimates are consistent with the already validated global central associations and prior conditional/main-effect results. There is therefore no evidence of context-dependent reversal or scientifically meaningful attenuation in these log-PFS or age extremes. I accept H144 through H152. The critical caveat is that these are unadjusted Welch associations within selected strata. log-PFS selection and age selection are not randomized; conditioning can in principle induce confounding or collider-like artifacts, and feature_019 is missing for 444 participants, so age-extreme claims apply only to the observed-age subset. Predictor labels are opaque and outcome is composite, so none of these findings supports a mechanism or causal interpretation. Multiplicity is a consideration across the broader run, but these particular estimates are extraordinarily large and their lower confidence bounds remain far above the effect-size threshold, making chance false acceptance implausible for these context-persistence claims. I request independent validation only for H146, the smallest and most attenuated of the accepted new context contrasts (feature_002 in the short log-PFS extreme). This gives a focused check on the most context-sensitive boundary case while avoiding redundant validation of the already-validated central signals.",
