trast may become positive, i.e. feature_063=1 associated with higher outcome_001 and weaker dependency. The reversed feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction in high feature_038 directly tests the raw positive interaction implied by the rejected negative-direction H189. Finally, the middle feature_038 band tests whether a reverse feature_063 association exists outside the extreme feature_038 quartiles, helping distinguish an average effect from an effect confined to feature_038 extremes. For direction -1 direct feature_063 claims, a positive signed estimate means feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001; for direction +1 direct claims, a positive signed estimate means feature_063=1 associated with higher outcome_001. These remain observational Welch comparisons in the supplied dataset with opaque predictor labels, overlapping subgroups, and no assigned biological roles; they do not establish causality, mechanism, or generalizability beyond the supplied and independent validation samples.",
