re_010 effect within feature_041=1 (H112), and marginal feature_037 and feature_002 effects within the opposite binary complement (H130,H131). I also registered two future claims because the current registered set lacks the global high-feature_018/high-feature_038 reverse direct contrast and the clean low-feature_038/high-feature_018 cell needed for a complete 2x2. These will be analyzed only if they enter the ledger. All requested analyses are observational Welch comparisons in the supplied dataset; expected valid cells are checked from variable counts, but any invalid cell will yield no conclusion. Direction must be interpreted as registered: for direction -1, positive signed values mean feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001, i.e. stronger composite dependency; for direction +1, positive signed values mean higher outcome_001, i.e. weaker dependency. No causal or biological role is claimed.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted core: feature_010=1 associated with higher outcome_001 by about +0.83 discovery/+0.82 validation; feature_002=1 by about +0.81/+0.85; feature_037=1 associated with lower outcome_001 by about -0.80 raw, accepted as reverse claim. Pairwise interactions among these dominant predictors are mostly null, including H134/H135. Feature_063 is the secondary reverse predictor: feature_063=1 often associated with lower outcome_001, especially in high feature_038 contexts. Feature_038 modification of feature_063 is validated globally (H177), in dominant-zero background (H187), and among feature_010=0 (H188). H166 global reverse remains unresolved active because R126 signed +0.239 lower +0.145, just below threshold; still a possible validation target. H208 now accepted active using existing R149: within feature_038>=0, positive feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction signed +0.638 lower +0.377, meaning high feature_018 attenuates the reverse feature_063 contrast. H200 deferred pending cleaner 2x2 contrasts. This iteration runs: H203 clean 0/0/0 low18/low38 reverse; H204 clean 0/0/0 high18/high38 reverse; H202 global low18/low38 reverse; H205 global high18/low38 reverse; H206 low18/upper38 reverse; H207 upper18/high38 positive direct; H209 middle38 band reverse. These should clarify whether feature_063 has an average reverse effect or is context dependent on feature_038 and feature_018. Also runs H136/H137 dominant predictors with median log_pfs, H112 feature_010 within feature_041=1, and H130/H131 marginal feature_037 and feature_002 effects in complements. Registered future claims: global high18/high38 reverse linked to H196/R157 and clean low38/high18 reverse linked to H186/R146. Continue cautious interpretation: many overlapping subgroup tests, no validation for most direct cells, opaque labels, and no mechanism.",
