  "narrative": "The new comparisons mostly decompose the feature_063 association and reinforce the dominant predictor set. For feature_063, the clean dominant-zero low-feature_018/low-feature_038 reverse contrast H203 is very weak (signed +0.031, lower -0.069), and the global low-feature_018/low-feature_038 contrast H202 is also weak and imprecise (signed +0.059, lower -0.086); both fail the 0.15-unit threshold and are rejected. This argues against a general low-feature_018 reverse effect independent of high feature_038. The global high-feature_018/low-feature_038 contrast H205 is not even in the reverse direction as registered (signed -0.113, lower -0.274), so it is rejected. By contrast, the low-feature_018/upper-feature_038 reverse contrast H206 is strong and precise (signed +0.866, lower +0.644), so I accept and close it. The clean dominant-zero high-feature_018/high-feature_038 reverse contrast H204 is above threshold but only barely (signed +0.303, lower +0.155) and has only 29 exposed observations; I accept it cautiously and keep it active rather than closing it. The upper-feature_018/high-feature_038 positive-direction contrast H207 is null or imprecisely negative (signed -0.040), so I reject it as evidence that feature_063=1 would be associated with higher outcome_001 in that cell. The middle feature_038 band reverse contrast H209 is suggestive but not threshold-robust (signed +0.240, lower +0.112), so it remains unresolved and active.\n\nThe dominant predictor analyses are consistent: H112 shows the accepted feature_010 positive association persists strongly within feature_041=1 (signed +0.914, lower +0.781); H130 and H131 confirm the feature_037 reverse and feature_002 positive associations in opposite binary complements (both lower bounds >0.73). The log_pfs interaction tests H136 and H137 are null or below threshold, so there is no evidence for meaningful modification by the median split of log_pfs_months.\n\nMultiplicity remains large because these are many overlapping subgroup contrasts, and small exposed cells occur in the feature_063 decomposition. I request validation of H166 because the key unresolved question is whether feature_063 has an average reverse association in the dataset at all. Its discovery estimate is +0.239 but the lower bound is +0.145, just below the 0.15 threshold; independent validation would decide whether to accept an average reverse effect or interpret feature_063 as primarily context-dependent. All conclusions remain observational associations in this dataset with opaque labels and no causal or biological role.",
  "validate": "H166",
  "research_notes": "Dominant dataset structure remains strong and stable: feature_010=1 associated with higher outcome_001 (~+0.83 discovery, +0.82 validation); feature_002=1 associated with higher outcome_001 (~+0.81 discovery, +0.85 validation); feature_037=1 associated with lower outcome_001 (~-0.80 raw; accepted reverse signed ~+0.80 discovery/validation). Pairwise interactions among these dominant predictors are mostly null, and log_pfs median interactions H136/H137 are now rejected. H112 accepts feature_010 effect within feature_041=1 (signed +0.914 lower +0.781). H130/H131 accept dominant-predictor effects in opposite complements: feature_037 reverse within feature_002=0 (signed +0.796 lower +0.739), feature_002 positive within feature_037=0 (signed +0.809 lower +0.749).\n\nFeature_063 is the main secondary predictor and is context dependent. Strong validated feature_038 modification remains central: H177 (global feature_063-by-feature_038 reverse interaction), H187 (dominant-zero background interaction), and H188 (feature_010=0 interaction) are accepted and validated. New feature_018-by-feature_038 direct contrasts clarify the average structure: global low18/low38 reverse H202 and clean dominant-zero low18/low38 reverse H203 are null/rejected, showing low feature_018 alone is not sufficient for a reverse feature_063 effect. Global high18/low38 reverse H205 is rejected (signed estimate negative). Low18/upper38 reverse H206 is very strong and accepted closed (signed +0.866 lower +0.644). Clean dominant-zero high18/high38 reverse H204 is accepted but active because lower bound is barely above threshold (+0.155) and exposed n=29. Upper18/high38 positive direct H207 is rejected. Middle feature_038 band H209 is unresolved active: signed +0.240 but lower +0.112, below threshold, though positive.\n\nGlobal feature_063 reverse average H166 remains unresolved active and has been selected for independent validation because R126 is borderline (signed +0.239 lower +0.145). If validation succeeds, feature_063 can be treated as having an average reverse dataset effect in addition to context modification; if it fails, the safer conclusion is that feature_063 is mainly a context-specific reverse predictor, strongest in high feature_038/low feature_018 or upper-feature_038 contexts, with attenuation among high feature_018 contexts. Pending/active unresolved feature_063 cells include H209, H210 global high18/high38 reverse, H211 clean dominant-zero low38/high18 reverse, H168/H169/H170/H176 borderline interactions or direct contrasts, and H191/H192 extreme feature_018 interaction acceptances with small cells. Many binary/categorical/numeric screens remain null; all conclusions are observational dataset-specific associations without causal, mechanistic, or generalizable interpretation."
