 and feature_015 show no meaningful average association; many other opaque predictors and categorical levels are null; positive feature_063 sign-reversal tests are not supported, including H219 in the clean upper-quartile feature_018 context; feature_019 median does not meaningfully modify feature_010; low-feature_018 reverse effects are not supported when feature_038 is low; pairwise dominant-predictor interactions are not supported. Unresolved uncertainty: the global feature_063 reverse average H166 remains unresolved because discovery R126 and validation R175 both have point estimates above threshold but adjusted lower bounds just below it; this is suggestive but not threshold-robust. Central-band H209 and high-feature_018 contexts H210, H213, H221, and H223 remain unresolved, indicating that attenuation of feature_063 at higher feature_018 is plausible but not conclusively established. Several accepted feature_063 contrasts remain active because of small exposed cells, borderline lower bounds, or discovery-only evidence. Most informative next analysis: I registered a new direct test of whether the reverse feature_063 association persists in a broad high-feature_018, central-feature_038 background, refining unresolved clean high-feature_018 central-band evidence. This avoids another global average test and asks whether high feature_018 attenuates the effect even outside the exact dominant-zero eligibility. If accepted, it broadens feature_063 relevance; if null or subthreshold, it supports the interpretation that feature_063 is mainly an amplifier within favorable feature_038/low-feature_018 contexts. Existing unanalyzed dominant-background contrasts H211, H215, and H216 are also useful for decomposition. All conclusions are associations in this dataset with opaque predictor labels; validation supports reproducibility in an independent sample but does not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability.",
