  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due. The accepted dataset structure remains three large, reproducible dominant associations: feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 by roughly +0.82 to +0.85 composite units, feature_002=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 by roughly +0.81 to +0.85 units, and feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 by roughly -0.80 raw units. These tested interactions among the dominant predictors are null, supporting an approximately additive dominant structure. The unresolved secondary question is feature_063: the reverse association, meaning feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001 and stronger dependency, is robust in many feature_038-high and feature_018-low contexts, but it attenuates near zero or subthreshold in high-feature_018 contexts and in some central-feature_038 contexts. The global feature_063 reverse average remains suggestive but not threshold-robust. I therefore avoid another global average test and register targeted context refinements.\n\nFirst, I propose a broad feature_010=0 restriction within the central feature_038 band. This tests whether the central-band lower bound is pulled toward subthreshold by the strong positive feature_010 contrast, or whether the central-band feature_063 reverse association is genuinely weaker. Second, I split that feature_010=0 central-band test into feature_018 nonnegative versus nonpositive contexts. This distinguishes feature_018 attenuation from central-band masking: if the reverse association is robust in low feature_018 but attenuated in high feature_018, the central-band evidence is likely a mixture of a real low-feature_018 effect and a high-feature_018 null. Third, I propose the analogous broad high-feature_018 central-band contrast without feature_010 restriction to assess whether the high-feature_018 attenuation persists in the full population, not only after exact dominant-zero or feature_010=0 conditioning. Fourth, I propose a low-feature_018, nonnegative-feature_036 contrast to test whether another standardized research signature defines an additional favorable context for the reverse feature_063 association.\n\nFor the dominant predictors, I register interaction tests between feature_010 or feature_002 and feature_063. These use positive direction to ask whether the dominant positive association is stronger in the feature_063=1 background, which could indicate compensatory nonadditivity or floor-like compression in lower-outcome backgrounds. Additivity predicts near zero, so anticipated direction is uncertain; these are effect-modification probes. Plausible alternatives include near-additivity, weak positive interaction, or unmeasured confounding by correlated dominant predictors. All central-band and feature_010=0 restrictions are expected to have enough exposed and comparator cells, but I will interpret any modest exposed cell cautiously.\n\nNo new independent validation is available, so acceptance will rely on discovery evidence. A newly proposed claim should be accepted only if its signed lower confidence limit exceeds the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction. Claims with point estimates above threshold but lower limits below it will remain unresolved unless cached or scheduled validation already exists. All conclusions remain observational associations in this supplied dataset with opaque predictor labels, overlapping subgroup definitions, multiple testing, and no assigned biological mechanism, causality, or generalizability beyond the supplied and already-validated samples."
