R6 give narrow intervals near zero with estimates below threshold (H4, H5, H6). This is a clean negative result.   For feature_063, the evidence supports a highly context-dependent reverse association rather than a uniform global effect. The global reverse association under direction -1 is directionally consistent but unresolved because both discovery and validation lower bounds are just below 0.15: discovery +0.239 lower +0.145 and validation +0.285 lower +0.146 (H166, R126/R175); the opposite global positive raw direction is rejected (H47, R126/R175). In contrast, conditional reverse associations are robust. In a clean dominant-zero background, feature_063 = 1 is associated with lower outcome_001 by +0.252 lower +0.169 in discovery and +0.352 lower +0.220 in validation (H165, R116/R125). The reverse association is strongest when feature_038 is nonnegative: direct feature_038 >= 0 +0.546 lower +0.408 (H178, R139), and the feature_038 >= 0 interaction +0.575 lower +0.400 in discovery and +0.667 lower +0.420 in validation (H177, R137/R138). It is also strongest when feature_018 is low: feature_018 <= 0 +0.454 lower +0.321 (H195, R156), clean dominant-zero low feature_018 +0.398 lower +0.271 (H201, R160), and feature_038 >= 0 together with low feature_018 +0.849 lower +0.671 (H197, R158). Conversely, feature_018 >= 0 attenuates the reverse association: signed positive attenuation interaction +0.429 lower +0.247 (H198, R143). Thus feature_063 should not be interpreted as a simple main-effect predictor; its measured association is modified by feature_038 and feature_018 context.   The latest feature_003 and feature_063-modifier screens largely refine rather than extend the model. The feature_003 reverse probes do not establish a threshold-reliable association: H274 and H276 are rejected because the full signed intervals fall below threshold (R234/R236); H275 and H278 remain unresolved with point estimates above or near threshold but lower bounds too low (R235/R238); H27