pproximate additivity or modest attenuation than with strong context dependence. I closed these investigations because there is little reason to continue slicing these particular interactions without independent validation. H293 is rejected: the feature_010 interaction with feature_025 has an entirely subthreshold signed interval and actually points toward attenuation rather than claimed enhancement. H294 and H295 remain unresolved because their upper bounds slightly cross 0.15, but their point estimates are weak and they should be treated only as incidental, unconfirmed possible modifications. H296 and H297 are rejected: feature_019 median context does not support claimed threshold-relevant modification of the feature_002 or feature_037 associations; their signed intervals are entirely below 0.15, and H297 is directionally negative.\n\nOverall, these results support continued caution. The accepted feature_063 contexts now include feature_033=1 and feature_060=1, but feature_003, feature_036, feature_025, feature_004, feature_026, and feature_019 do not establish robust new threshold-relevant modifiers of the dominant predictors. Since validation requests are exhausted, all conclusions remain observational associations in this supplied dataset, not causal, mechanistic, biological, or generalizable claims. I activated the remaining well-powered untested binary main-effect screens (H45, H46, H48-H56, H100) to complete broader exploration of measured predictors rather than continue small-cell feature_063 refinement.",
