ro or rejected. The best current structure is therefore approximate additive marginal associations rather than strong pairwise interaction among feature_010, feature_002, feature_037, and feature_027. These conclusions remain dataset-specific and are not multivariable-adjusted or causal.\n\nFeature_063 remains best described as context-dependent rather than globally resolved. The global reverse association is directionally consistent but unresolved: signed +0.239 discovery lower +0.145 (H166/R126) and signed +0.285 validation lower +0.146 (R175), both just below the 0.15 threshold. The opposite global direction is rejected (H47). Conditional reverse associations are well supported: clean dominant-zero background (H165/R116/R125), feature_010=0 (H167/R127), feature_037=0 (H171/R131), feature_002=0 (H172/R132), feature_038 nonnegative (H178/R139 and validated interaction H177/R137/R138), low feature_018 contexts (H195/R156, H201/R160), and especially feature_018<=0 with feature_038>=0 (H197/R158). The clean interaction evidence in feature_038 nonnegative and feature_010=0 also validates (H188/R148/R151). In low feature_018 contexts, feature_063 also shows validated interaction stability (H187/R147/R162). Thus, feature_063 should be interpreted as an effect whose relevance depends strongly on measured context, especially feature_038 and feature_018.\n\nNEGATIVE AND NULL FINDINGS. The constructed research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 show no meaningful average association (H4/R4, H5/R5, H6/R6). Broad recent screens rejected feature_060, feature_035, feature_033, feature_013, feature_064 in the claimed direction, feature_022, feature_028, feature_043, and feature_050 as threshold-relevant main effects. Most other tested binary and categorical contrasts, including many feature_024, feature_034, feature_046, feature_052, feature_054, feature_059, feature_061, and feature_062 levels, are near zero or have signed intervals below the 0.15 threshold. Inter